From cd08686dc07353a55b61692e8ed9e1356f470f69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:28:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] soc: qcom: smp2p: fix remoteproc restart issue

A kick is required to start the SMP2P communicating process in Q6.

For the first boot, qcom_smp2p_probe() will do this.

But in the remain restart sequence, the driver is waiting the interruption
from the slave-kernel channel while the Q6 is waiting the kick to set the
smem-state. So the restart proccess always timeouts.

Here we check the slave-kernel value. The default 0 value mean Q6 has
restarted and is waiting for the kick. After kick sent, Q6 will set the
ready bit, so the value becomes non-zero.

Signed-off-by: Ziyang Huang <hzyitc@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -273,6 +273,10 @@ static void qcom_smp2p_notify_in(struct
 				handle_nested_irq(irq_pin);
 			}
 		}
+
+		if (val == 0)
+			/* Q6 has restarted, kick as required. */
+			qcom_smp2p_kick(smp2p);
 	}
 }
 
